{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730070Z","id":"47eb01b7fd5fc3eb85b2d44bde1ae8b41029603afd1dda5c7f5fb072411419ac","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:114 (Q1)): doctor prints the approval line and never writes it. Writing it needs a comment-preserving TOML edit in clax init and a matching removal in clax uninit; the doctor's mcp detail and the READMEs then change.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":459},"end":{"line":461},"content_hash":"ab384b31d810513ba2793692a27f8dac0f9118459eeaf07fe63eb2939829ea9f"},"summary":"Have clax init write Grok's tool approval, MCPTool(clax_grok__*), into ~/.grok/config.toml","tags":["revisit:the owner wants clax init to lift Grok's per-call approval","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor_agent.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.730170Z","id":"913befb96284920adcabfe68b2fb7927291da171c7a5df898fa5236a66365606","body":{"detail":"Not taken (2026-10-01, docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-01-grok-build.md:113 (Q3)): Grok Build 1.0.45 and later, warned by doctor only (MIN_GROK). A different minimum changes this warning and the contract's measurement line; enforcing it would add a version check to the shim or the hooks.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":550},"end":{"line":552},"content_hash":"08f4786b8e87c9b1ee9c6633438a61b1ef298ae07c9c75f84ab8067ba94831bc"},"summary":"Enforce a minimum Grok Build version instead of warning in doctor only","tags":["revisit:a Grok Build release older than MIN_GROK breaks Clax in the field","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:18:44.697602Z","id":"953ed568ee63d900d24099459ad9eac9cefb3b71428050791cb057b21f68208e","body":{"detail":"Failure: after an upgrade, before the daemon is replaced, `clax doctor` runs Store::open, which plans and records the backfill (seconds on a large home, with no progress shown). Changes the still-running older daemon makes after that plan are never recorded: they are not in the staging snapshot, and the older build records nothing live.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":613},"end":{"line":613},"content_hash":"e8cfaa20dc14468f4bef01aba5ada983db7554d9886c28787dbaec157f0587e0"},"suggested_fix":"Have doctor and init open the store without the backfill (or read-only) when the schema is behind and a daemon is running, and leave the backfill to the daemon's start, which reports progress.","summary":"clax doctor (and clax init's credential revoke) open the store directly, so the first run of a new build migrates to 23 and runs the whole backfill outside the daemon, silently, possibly under an older running daemon","tags":["review","migration","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:06:06.687692Z","id":"d2386e4668a1db08b83107394256621eb35a796e99cf86d2e5d8060ff546220f","body":{"detail":"Spec section 6.7 has a remote person's `agents` and `status` list the person's own agents through GET /api/agents, which plan Task 16 adds; it does not exist yet. GET /api/sessions?live=true answers a grant with its own grant's sessions only, so a person with two machines sees one machine's agents, and the owner sees the token's sessions. Switch agents_of to GET /api/agents when Task 16 lands; crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs remote_cli_commands_work_as_listed asserts the listing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"035c183d3a6be59d25aaa64b5804fd572d3599590675c6439571b9ea7a6f1271"},"summary":"clax agents and the remote clax status list this credential's sessions through GET /api/sessions, not the person's agents through GET /api/agents","tags":["spec:6.7","revisit:GET /api/agents exists","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/connect.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:06:06.687756Z","id":"53080db307210215f653922a96822d22d16804a28173b33faa7b39cc51d91526","body":{"detail":"The continuation that issues tokens also rotates the continuation token, so a poll whose answer is lost leaves the client with a token the daemon no longer knows (401 invalid_token, or 409 already_issued). clax connect then forgets the request and its key and tells the person to have the owner revoke the connection in People; the next connect makes a new key and request. The stray grant signs nothing without the key. A retry that re-issues to the same key (an idempotent issue) would let the client recover without the owner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":353},"end":{"line":361},"content_hash":"38a5aeac6bc7aaf40772b6316b28717047bfaf09232aa277f3bb3826a9b77aca"},"summary":"A request whose tokens were issued to an answer that never arrived cannot be finished: its grant stays live until the owner revokes it or 30 days pass","tags":["spec:6.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/connect.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T15:45:51.492338Z","id":"672e8ed0336b2436832365a5e5941505628838622e507ecf33ce60da41456ad6","body":{"detail":"The continuation that issues tokens also rotates the continuation token, so a poll whose answer is lost on the wire leaves the client with a token the daemon no longer knows (401 invalid_token, or 409 already_issued). clax connect then forgets the request and its key and tells the person to have the owner revoke the connection in People; the next connect makes a new key and request. The stray grant signs nothing without the key. An answer that did arrive is never lost here: remote-pending.json is removed only after remote.json is saved (both written whole by write_private). Recovery today needs the owner.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":406},"end":{"line":414},"content_hash":"38a5aeac6bc7aaf40772b6316b28717047bfaf09232aa277f3bb3826a9b77aca"},"suggested_fix":"Idempotent re-issue: keep the hash of the pre-issue continuation token until the access token is first used (at most 10 minutes); a continuation call presenting it, signed by the grant's key with a later t, revokes the undelivered tokens and issues fresh ones in one transaction. Safe because the tokens are key-bound: a sniffer of the old token cannot sign, and accept_t refuses a replay.","summary":"A request whose tokens were issued to an answer that never arrived cannot be finished: its grant stays live until the owner revokes it or 30 days pass","supersedes":"53080db307210215f653922a96822d22d16804a28173b33faa7b39cc51d91526","tags":["spec:6.3","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/doctor.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T16:50:12.003308Z","id":"30b40937db6fcc6853c2e891eb74d41c5867833b9f9dfdc786dfaacb3f9b465b","body":{"detail":"Failure: after an upgrade, before the daemon is replaced, `clax doctor` runs Store::open, which plans and records the backfill (seconds on a large home, with no progress shown). Changes the still-running older daemon makes after that plan are never recorded: they are not in the staging snapshot, and the older build records nothing live.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":730},"end":{"line":730},"content_hash":"e8cfaa20dc14468f4bef01aba5ada983db7554d9886c28787dbaec157f0587e0"},"suggested_fix":"Have doctor and init open the store without the backfill (or read-only) when the schema is behind and a daemon is running, and leave the backfill to the daemon's start, which reports progress.","summary":"clax doctor (and clax init's credential revoke) open the store directly, so the first run of a new build migrates to 23 and runs the whole backfill outside the daemon, silently, possibly under an older running daemon","supersedes":"953ed568ee63d900d24099459ad9eac9cefb3b71428050791cb057b21f68208e","tags":["review","migration","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T18:38:30.048361Z","id":"00bea6fae2fdd9fb28a20ca6ee09153693fae7af98765bc2152d1c26090067c2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:53dde86","summary":"Fixed: agents_of and Client::probe_remote read GET /api/agents and keep the person's own live agents; crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs remote_cli_commands_work_as_listed asserts Sam's agent alone is listed and passes (cargo test -p clax-cli).","supersedes":"d2386e4668a1db08b83107394256621eb35a796e99cf86d2e5d8060ff546220f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.263051Z","id":"4ff569eb4ea2c56cae94c692844d83ce73830b5559aaf2100195bc88ba50c168","body":{"detail":"A grant's path session needs X-Clax-Session (400 no_session) and, since spec 2026-10-08 §6.8, that session's X-Clax-Session-Secret (401 invalid_session_proof). Remote follow was not wired for either before this change. Plan Task 19 (remote agent sides) should read the credential file for (--agent, --harness-session) or GROK_SESSION_ID with clax_core::remote::SessionFiles, as crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs RemoteSession does, and send both headers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":137},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"efceb9f41d50794ae50088e62cbe938520b343e7c96da6d364c3319f2f984da3"},"summary":"clax feedback follow in remote mode names its session only in the path, without X-Clax-Session or the session's secret","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:12:47.263116Z","id":"5d0c97a9762596ba8578af4ce584495f8369846040c2bb6d8f012323e061ccba","body":{"detail":"RemoteSession::keys falls back to <harness>-ppid-<parent PID>.json (and ancestors), which spec 2026-10-08 §6.8 needs for Codex, whose shim learns no harness session ID. In a Claude Code process whose session ID changed (/clear), the new ID's hooks find the shim's parent-PID file and act as the shim's session (proved_row in crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs refreshes the proved row), where a local hook would join a new hook-only row. Arguably what the agent wants (the same MCP server serves it), but it differs from local mode.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":298},"end":{"line":314},"content_hash":"5cf3d3f639cbda5f86884a701650fc0b9c3e1e75b5f9a4410d020f4b71cbb35d"},"summary":"A remote hook with no credential file for its harness session ID acts as the session its parent's file names","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.637702Z","id":"08ef165bed738842a0f23d9f0ad5be89d1b4a550c34067c06267f91a6a18abb2","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5d0c97a9762596ba8578af4ce584495f8369846040c2bb6d8f012323e061ccba","span":{"start":{"line":298},"end":{"line":314},"content_hash":"5cf3d3f639cbda5f86884a701650fc0b9c3e1e75b5f9a4410d020f4b71cbb35d"},"summary":"The PID fallback reaches past this harness's own process: the ancestor walk finds an outer agent's ppid file (an agent run from another agent's shell), and a stale ppid file of a crashed harness whose session is still live is found by a new process with the reused PID; see the concern on crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:339-355 (proved_row) for the reproduced server half and a fix.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638532Z","id":"64fd9bb20b8011cb641184d4219833e9bafc0900f181a228b92eb121c8bbd21b","body":{"detail":"Spec §6.8 (Clients) says the hook waits up to one second for the file and retries once. The loop at lines 452-476 waits again after every refused retry: a file that keeps changing (a shim re-registering, a stale file replaced) gives a second and later one-second wait, so the hook's time is bounded only by the hook's own deadline. No test covers the wait: making wait_for_credential return at once fails no test in crates/clax-cli/tests (connect.rs).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":452},"end":{"line":540},"content_hash":"44916c0724862857eb5566da961637d1a2fc65fb6bf90ea78396c66e85ed7a35"},"suggested_fix":"Wait at most once per hook run (a flag), then fail with the refusal; add a connect.rs test that starts the hook while a shim writes the file after a delay.","summary":"The SessionStart join's wait for a credential file can retry more than once and is untested","tags":["review","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.895954Z","id":"c4e7b0447c4c4665c8ffcad2fe204fea99dbdae52cd97dd8c39fb27ac424d81b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"A hook now takes a parent-PID file only as join would match its row (SessionFiles::find: a row with no harness session ID, or the hook's own) and only while that PID names the process recorded in the file, so after /clear, or for an agent nested in another's shell, the hooks no longer act as the shim's or the parent's session. Evidence: remote::session_file_tests::a_parent_pid_file_is_taken_only_as_join_would_match_and_by_the_same_process, connect::a_nested_agents_hook_never_becomes_its_parents_session and connect::a_codex_hook_finds_its_shims_session_by_its_parent_and_never_by_a_reused_pid pass.","supersedes":"5d0c97a9762596ba8578af4ce584495f8369846040c2bb6d8f012323e061ccba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.900021Z","id":"0834271ac6f15f747dc8d9b3f28bcece27c1a0e7fbedf3a934e8b547dcc6cf14","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"The join's attempts are join_attempts: the found credential, then none, then one wait and one retry, as spec §6.8 now says. Evidence: hook::join_tests::a_live_row_without_a_proof_waits_once_and_retries_once (wait called once; a refused waited credential is not waited for again) and a_found_credential_is_used_and_a_stale_one_dropped pass; the no-wait mutation is caught.","supersedes":"64fd9bb20b8011cb641184d4219833e9bafc0900f181a228b92eb121c8bbd21b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:07:51.982540Z","id":"f9d403db3883c730799609147c7e7100e2928da6c52226534787f7d7dbe39656","body":{"detail":"Two mutations pass every clax-cli test: RemoteSession::pids returning only the parent (no ancestors), so a hook run through a wrapper shell never finds its shim's file under its grandparent; and wait_for_credential returning a credential the join just refused, so a stale file wins the wait at once and the join fails instead of waiting for the shim's new file. join_tests stub the wait with a closure, so the real function is never called.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":558},"end":{"line":575},"content_hash":"65a9ea069595ccfa57fbed1e14b06c63407e091d054d95e3da29c48f474e98fc"},"suggested_fix":"Add a connect test whose hook runs under a wrapper shell with the shim's file keyed by the grandparent; add a unit test calling wait_for_credential over a SessionFiles that holds the refused credential and then a new one (written before the call, no sleep).","summary":"The hook's ancestor walk for parent-PID files and wait_for_credential's refused filter are untested","tags":["review","tests","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:51:49.482829Z","id":"b958cd96454809f9734a9b5f3dbf1543160abb7b432a47855539d77ff5fa8ed2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a8d0a534","summary":"Both paths are tested: connect::a_hook_behind_a_wrapper_shell_finds_its_shims_session_by_an_ancestor runs the hook under /bin/sh so the shim's file is under its grandparent (kills MU15), and hook::remote_session_tests::the_wait_takes_a_new_credential_never_the_refused_one calls the real wait_for_credential over SessionFiles holding the refused credential, then a new one, with a zero bound (kills MU10). Evidence: target/t19a/mutations3.txt.","supersedes":"f9d403db3883c730799609147c7e7100e2928da6c52226534787f7d7dbe39656","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T07:20:43.737142Z","id":"c308033f74ae7ac639f827b93e618dc0e998c3a77c24162e47fe54d87bbfe7df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9be93c11","summary":"Remote follow reads the session's credential (by harness session file, or by session ID through SessionFiles::by_session) and sends X-Clax-Session and X-Clax-Session-Secret on the listing and notices requests; a Clax session with no credential fails with session_credential_missing. Evidence: connect::remote_follow_names_its_session_with_its_proof passes; with the proof headers removed it times out.","supersedes":"4ff569eb4ea2c56cae94c692844d83ce73830b5559aaf2100195bc88ba50c168","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.319399Z","id":"782c5bfb0624dce80ef7040b6603b0e3761e9cd9bfe5e6b72ec3d26c2623d00d","body":{"detail":"Failure: Sam's Claude Code on a connected machine, on a slow network; a batch of three comments on three threads with clips is sent to it. The prompt hook (PROMPT_DEADLINE 4 s, FEEDBACK_REQUEST_TIMEOUT 3 s per request, hook.rs:30-32) lists sessions, takes the feedback (GET /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback?tier=prompt_hook marks the rows delivered), then remote_text GETs each clip in turn. At about 1.5 s a clip the worker overruns the deadline, run() prints nothing ('timed out after 4s'), and the comments reach the agent only as a resend, at least Store::RESEND_AFTER_SECS (120 s) later and only on the Stop hook or piggyback tiers. Several comments in one thread name the same clip and are fetched again each time (the shim's fetch_clips in crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs dedupes; this closure does not).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":557},"end":{"line":578},"content_hash":"1c0282ad2134ccf1b1f23d08181e1e9b0331fc871296cccfe008f1f8923bc412"},"suggested_fix":"Dedupe references as fetch_clips does, and stop fetching once the remaining budget is under one request timeout, rewriting the rest to `Clip: unavailable (no time left in the hook)`; or bound every clip GET by what is left of budget(agent, event).0.","summary":"A remote hook fetches every clip its payload names, one after another and once per Clip: line, inside the hook's deadline, after the take already handed the rows over","tags":["review","remote","hooks","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:02:04.320076Z","id":"c71d8f9aebb7d1475c3ebfb5b6f7275690da26d6463a7c88574031373055d723","body":{"detail":"Mutation: dropping `|| m.starts_with(\"invalid_session_proof:\")` from session_gone; the follow and connect tests (100) all passed. By reading, a harness-target follower rereads the credential file every loop, so a session registered again under the same harness session ID is followed; with the mutant the follower backs off forever instead of exiting after its grace when a stale credential file outlives its session. connect::remote_follow_names_its_session_with_its_proof covers only --once against a live session.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":161},"content_hash":"c9afcd52c5dc17eb03b9bb9f769094d118ef168a35822d6fb97b2c275563454e"},"suggested_fix":"Add a connect test that ends the session, rewrites the credential file with a new registration, and checks the follower delivers the next notice; and one where the stale file stays and the follower exits after --grace.","summary":"Remote follow's handling of a refused proof (invalid_session_proof) and of a session restarting under it has no test","tags":["review","remote","tests","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.437414Z","id":"ed38a8148e03fb56a90c842bd7fe21a5f9c145cbbab6f6b7049d36c5e94e130f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"The hook fetches each distinct clip at once within what is left of its deadline less CLIP_MARGIN (clax_core::clips::fetch_within); a clip not back reads 'Clip: unavailable (timed out)' and the comments are printed. Evidence: connect::a_remote_hook_prints_its_comments_when_clips_do_not_come (a proxy that never answers clip requests; the prompt hook prints both comments within its 4 s deadline) and clips::tests::fetches_are_deduplicated_concurrent_and_bounded pass; with the bound lifted the hook test fails. The shim (remote::a_remote_clip_that_does_not_come_never_holds_the_feedback) and Pi (remote.test.ts 'a clip that does not come in time, or is not a PNG, never holds the comments') follow the same rule.","supersedes":"782c5bfb0624dce80ef7040b6603b0e3761e9cd9bfe5e6b72ec3d26c2623d00d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:55:01.438547Z","id":"229d2366f1d35437efd46336dab3b244b1da7b0d20a3203fe992281f3eb3fbb8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7a06e2cd","summary":"Evidence: connect::remote_follow_of_an_ended_session_exits and connect::remote_follow_follows_its_harness_session_across_a_restart pass; with invalid_session_proof dropped from session_gone the first fails (M4 killed).","supersedes":"c71d8f9aebb7d1475c3ebfb5b6f7275690da26d6463a7c88574031373055d723","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:16:36.714116Z","id":"3795ed68a0dd9421bb445a65dd90943ce3ac10e2062ff483193cbc2cccb73486","body":{"detail":"Mutations, each run against the connect, remote and clips tests: the hook's `clax_core::clips::check(ct.as_deref(), &bytes)?` replaced by a no-op survived; the shim's check in clip_bytes replaced by a no-op survived. clips::tests::a_clip_is_checked_before_it_is_kept tests check() alone, and only Pi's remote.test.ts serves a non-PNG clip.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":607},"end":{"line":607},"content_hash":"8cc42c560ef2a439d5a9af5ecb2cce73595dfed3e5b1e6ddd18358b69affce8b"},"suggested_fix":"Serve one clip as text/html (or as image/png without the PNG signature) in connect::a_remote_hook_prints_its_comments_when_clips_do_not_come and remote::a_remote_clip_that_does_not_come_never_holds_the_feedback, and assert `Clip: unavailable (not a PNG)`.","summary":"No Rust test reaches the clip check in either client: removing clips::check from the hook's fetch, or from the shim's clip_bytes (crates/clax-mcp/src/client.rs:1203), passes every test","tags":["review","tests","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:16:49.647638Z","id":"dfa824810ece91e919c2d89ac93fdb6b704da57bee6becdffd5df2e435589b7e","body":{"detail":"tracing_subscriber::fmt() turns on log_internal_errors, which eprintln!s a failed write; eprintln! panics on EPIPE. When the harness exits while a tool call is in flight (wait_for_feedback, ask), the shim logs 'timed out draining in-flight responses' to the closed stderr pipe and panics before shim::run reaches client.end_session() (crates/clax-mcp/src/shim.rs:281). Reproduced with the built binary in remote mode: parent exits during a 60 s wait_for_feedback with stderr piped -> exit status 101, the session stays live and its credential files stay in remote-sessions/; the same run with stderr to a file ends the session (exit 0). The panic is in main's code too, but a local session has a pid the reaper probes (ended within 5 minutes); a remote session has none (spec 2026-10-08 §6.7) and holds its threads (others get thread_taken), its name and its place in Send menus for the 30-minute remote idle window.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":67},"end":{"line":75},"content_hash":"a759af09aa534bdc650eb91ca2173006e8d4e8540384fc5d52115c190a3ac18e"},"suggested_fix":"Build the subscriber with .log_internal_errors(false) (or a writer that ignores EPIPE), and keep the end-of-session path free of anything that can panic on a closed stdio.","summary":"The shim panics (exit 101) when its stderr is gone and it logs a warning on the way out, so a remote session is never ended and stays live for 30 minutes","tags":["review","remote","lifecycle","final-review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/src/commands/mcp.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.140524Z","id":"dcac7d9d479a1faf698b165343cfd10fd231f1f17e5b46a047b2173c8a333917","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a3e5cc5c","summary":"Fixed in a3e5cc5c: the shim's tracing writer (QuietStderr) drops writes to a broken pipe and log_internal_errors is off. Evidence: connect::a_remote_shim_whose_stderr_closed_still_ends_its_session passes (RUST_LOG=info, stderr closed at spawn: exit 0, session ended, credential file removed); before the fix the shim died before answering initialize.","supersedes":"dfa824810ece91e919c2d89ac93fdb6b704da57bee6becdffd5df2e435589b7e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
